From: Azure Linux <azl-maintainers@microsoft.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cli: return success for informational options

Passing a string to sys.exit writes it to stderr and exits with status 1.
Print explicitly and return success only for help and version requests.

diff --git a/nbdime/__main__.py b/nbdime/__main__.py
--- a/nbdime/__main__.py
+++ b/nbdime/__main__.py
@@ -121,7 +121,9 @@ def main_dispatch(args=None):
     else:
         if cmd == '--version':
-            sys.exit(__version__)
+            print(__version__)
+            return 0
         if cmd == '-h' or cmd == '--help':
-            sys.exit(HELP_MESSAGE_VERBOSE)
+            print(HELP_MESSAGE_VERBOSE)
+            return 0
         if cmd == '--config':
             # List all possible config options:
